Produce an execution-ready ownership and migration inventory for every backend-to-TUI data path, starting with src/ava/tui/runtime.h, app/tui/interactive_tui.cpp and its state_snapshot closure, runtime_state.*, runtime_active_run_internal.*, TuiFrontEnd.*, and app/frontend/*. Include initial TuiRuntimeOptions fields, callback return types, TuiSubmitResult, selector views, startup/trust/branch/subagent snapshots, transcript/tool events, permissions/questions, plugin UI and image/Mermaid bridges. Follow every producer and consumer, rather than searching only for names containing Snapshot.

For each path record its canonical backend owner, mutation sites, lifecycle, frontend projection owner, refresh outputs, coherence requirements, asynchronous/session authority, existing tests, and the later migration goal that removes it. Distinguish observable state from ordered event delivery, commands and correlated decisions, immutable construction dependencies, and strictly frontend-local rendering/editor caches. Explicitly identify backend types/includes currently exposed to TUI. The target boundary allows neutral contracts, not Session/store/coordinator access from TUI. Confirm ModelSelection and SessionStats registration, write notification, snapshot copying and independent changed flags as the reference implementation; identify necessary boundary cleanup without redesigning their behavior.

Store the inventory and acceptance matrix as plan artifacts with a contents entry. It must account for every transported Snapshot and every non-Snapshot state bypass, and identify concrete focused tests and real terminal scenarios. No migration is complete on the strength of a type rename. Resolve genuinely ambiguous event/interaction ownership before coding its slice; do not quietly exempt live backend state from the objective.
